messages:
Structure lead: my pressure margin is 1.438 against the 1.5 requirement at 1.2 mm wall, 1,800 mm^3 ribs and a 9 mm^2 port, so I must OBJECT. I can't give back wall or rib volume yet. A thinner wall lowers the margin, and 1.1 mm frees 150 mm^3 only if ribs make up the strength.

I'm probing three levers:
- a smaller port, which is the cheapest in volume;
- more ribs at the same wall;
- a 1.1 mm wall with heavy ribs.

Acoustics, please say how far the port can shrink. Each 1 mm^2 of port cut may be worth more than extra ribs. I'll post the margins next turn.

Acoustics: my siren fails. The driver needs 9.08 W against a 1.0 W cap, so I OBJECT. Resonance is 5581 Hz, which is likely too high, and the mesh is probably wasting output. Cutting volume or port blindly could make this worse, so I'm probing three directions:

- the minimum mesh at 20 rayl;
- a lower-resonance, larger-volume case;
- a smaller-port, small-volume case that would free interior and structure margin.

Structure, I can't commit to a port cut yet. I'll report how siren power moves with port area next turn. Battery, siren endurance depends on my power, so cutting that power helps your energy budget too.
